  "title": "Talking About Your Arrival",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "In the final lesson, combine regular and irregular participles with questions and travel language. Use the pretérito perfecto to describe what has happened during the trip so far. Choose the correct form of haber for the subject, then add the appropriate participle."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Hemos llegado por la mañana.",
          "english": "We have arrived in the morning."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Han visto las montañas.",
          "english": "They have seen the mountains."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Has reservado el hotel?",
          "english": "Have you booked the hotel?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Sí, he escrito la dirección.",
          "english": "Yes, I have written down the address."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "he / has / ha + -ado",
          "regular -ar participle"
        ],
        [
          "he / has / ha + -ido",
          "regular -er/-ir participle"
        ],
        [
          "he / has / ha + visto",
          "irregular participle"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Build the form in two steps: choose haber for the subject, then choose the correct participle."
